Displaced Avenger wrote:
> For YANI justification, I agree with John H.  Loadstones are
> magical--they couldn't auto-curse otherwise.  Remove curse doesn't
> change the nature of that magic, while this YANI would.  There are gray
> stones that are lighter than loadstones, and, of the three, flint is
> the most useless, so I figured that being able to turn a loadstone into
> a flint stone would not have any game-balance issues (it's a lot easier
> to get a bunch of rocks than a loadstone and a !oEnlightenment).  There
> are no other items which could be argued to be "magically heavy", so I
> don't think there's a precedent. 

	Cursed bags of holding, as someone else suggested elsethread.
However, to be consistent, this shouldn't uncurse them, it should turn
them into cursed sacks.

	I don't see that there's a balance problem here... potions of
enlightenment are harder to come by than holy water, and cost you
something to use, unlike some of the other ways to deal with a loadstone
or cursed BoH, which can be as little as a few points of Power or a
prayer timeout. And using it on a BoH would cost you a potentially
useful item in exchange for the ability to get at its contents safely
(and you still can't use it on one that you can't pick up).

	It's slightly but not tremendously useful, and it's a terrible
pun. I'm for it!

